WEBVTT

00:01:30.728 --> 00:01:32.313
<i>This Yanagawara Camp</i>

00:01:32.563 --> 00:01:34.773
<i>is used as CAAC Special Forces' base</i>

00:01:34.982 --> 00:01:37.610
<i>whenever they enter the Area.</i>

00:01:38.444 --> 00:01:40.779
<i>The Guillotine Shutter's electric shock</i>

00:01:40.863 --> 00:01:43.240
<i>has paralyzed the Matter in this area.</i>

00:01:43.824 --> 00:01:45.242
<i>It will be safe for now.</i>

00:01:49.204 --> 00:01:51.624
What? We can enter through the front?

00:01:55.336 --> 00:01:57.504
I haven't been here in a while.

00:01:57.588 --> 00:01:58.756
That's true.

00:01:58.964 --> 00:02:01.592
Who the heck is that guy anyway?

00:02:02.051 --> 00:02:03.093
I don't know.

00:02:11.894 --> 00:02:15.314
External insulation and circulation
systems checked.

00:02:16.065 --> 00:02:17.858
We can relax here for a bit.

00:02:25.407 --> 00:02:27.076
You can take off your suit.

00:02:32.206 --> 00:02:33.457
There's showers here.

00:02:34.166 --> 00:02:35.084
Yahoo!

00:02:35.876 --> 00:02:37.628
Watch my Live Suit, Haruka!

00:02:37.711 --> 00:02:38.962
Hey! Kaede!

00:02:41.382 --> 00:02:44.218
I tried, but I can't get it off.

00:02:44.802 --> 00:02:47.179
The separator has been activated,

00:02:47.596 --> 00:02:50.933
so the Live Suit must have
high affinity with your skin.

00:02:51.016 --> 00:02:53.268
Really? Is that so?

00:02:53.727 --> 00:02:56.063
I guess your suit is pretty fond of you.

00:02:57.439 --> 00:02:59.233
<i>That is everyone's duties.</i>

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:02.903
There are no more resupply points ahead.

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.446
Ensure you're well supplied.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:05.531
-Got it.
-Yessir.

00:03:05.948 --> 00:03:08.117
Minase, you're on guard duty.

00:03:08.951 --> 00:03:09.827
Yes, sir.

00:03:10.411 --> 00:03:11.578
-Excuse me.
-What?

00:03:12.079 --> 00:03:14.415
Can I accompany him?

00:03:14.998 --> 00:03:18.043
I want to get a good look at the Area.

00:03:18.377 --> 00:03:19.962
It's not safe!

00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:21.171
Join me!

00:03:21.964 --> 00:03:23.507
I'll be your bodyguard.

00:03:24.091 --> 00:03:25.008
Thank you.

00:03:25.092 --> 00:03:25.926
But...

00:03:26.009 --> 00:03:30.347
From what our sensors tell us,
this area is secure right now.

00:03:30.889 --> 00:03:32.099
If you're leading us

00:03:32.182 --> 00:03:35.853
to Primary Point, you should
be able to make a call like that.

00:03:47.656 --> 00:03:50.200
All right, we're going to need you now.

00:03:57.249 --> 00:03:58.125
<i>In human form?</i>

00:03:58.917 --> 00:04:02.212
Maybe the activity the other day
transformed the Matter.

00:04:02.588 --> 00:04:06.008
Or the transformation itself
caused the activity.

00:04:06.508 --> 00:04:09.678
<i>Anyway, I'll do what I can</i>
<i>to support you from here.</i>

00:04:10.012 --> 00:04:11.597
-Thanks.
-<i>Besides,</i>

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.808
<i>I was supposed to go to Tokyo,</i>
<i>but this makes things easier.</i>

00:04:15.184 --> 00:04:16.852
<i>I'll pay her a visit.</i>

00:04:18.103 --> 00:04:20.856
At any rate, I'll keep Hori in charge.

00:04:21.565 --> 00:04:25.027
<i>Keep me informed of what</i>
<i>happens in the capital.</i>

00:04:25.402 --> 00:04:26.278
<i>Bye.</i>

00:04:29.281 --> 00:04:31.617
I'm your ride, Superintendent Nanbara.

00:04:32.451 --> 00:04:34.536
I told them I didn't need a...

00:04:36.121 --> 00:04:38.957
Sorry, you're a director now, right?

00:04:39.708 --> 00:04:40.959
Kurose?

00:04:42.878 --> 00:04:47.549
<i>I didn't know that Divers have</i>
<i>such an amazing job.</i>

00:04:47.633 --> 00:04:50.761
<i>No, it's not as amazing</i>
<i>as you think, Tachibana.</i>

00:04:51.762 --> 00:04:52.805
Call me Aiko.

00:04:52.971 --> 00:04:54.723
Then call me Kazuki.

00:04:56.183 --> 00:04:58.435
-Aiko...
-Yes?

00:04:58.519 --> 00:04:59.728
So...

00:05:00.354 --> 00:05:02.439
What was it you said at K1?

00:05:03.899 --> 00:05:07.945
You need to get to Primary Point
to save your family? Is that true?

00:05:11.824 --> 00:05:13.075
Did I say too much?

00:05:13.659 --> 00:05:16.245
No. I'm sorry.

00:05:23.836 --> 00:05:25.837
Well, it's really quiet.

00:05:26.421 --> 00:05:28.840
That Guillotine sure is powerful.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:30.592
Why are you here?

00:05:30.676 --> 00:05:33.679
I was worried about you alone,
so I came to help.

00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:37.266
Aren't you and Seri
supposed to be resupplying?

00:05:38.433 --> 00:05:41.436
I get a lot more work done
without Kaede around.

00:05:41.937 --> 00:05:42.938
Look at all this.

00:05:43.021 --> 00:05:46.233
The government can do amazing things,
even in a hurry.

00:05:46.567 --> 00:05:48.360
These resources are incredible

00:05:49.361 --> 00:05:51.697
<i>Hydro, okay.</i>

00:05:52.322 --> 00:05:55.200
It's in pretty good shape
for being abandoned.

00:05:56.702 --> 00:05:57.703
Come in.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.871
You know...

00:06:00.539 --> 00:06:04.167
I'm amazed you're
carrying out this bold plan,

00:06:04.459 --> 00:06:05.669
Yuya Kanzaki.

00:06:06.920 --> 00:06:10.173
I never could have done it
without your cooperation.

00:06:11.967 --> 00:06:14.261
<i>As always, you have keen intuition.</i>

00:06:15.053 --> 00:06:18.640
<i>This is good timing.</i>
<i>Aiko Tachibana has gone missing.</i>

00:06:19.224 --> 00:06:21.018
You already know about it?

00:06:21.351 --> 00:06:23.812
It has sent the hospital into a flurry.

00:06:24.938 --> 00:06:25.981
Do you know anything?

00:06:26.565 --> 00:06:28.108
-No.
-I see.

00:06:28.984 --> 00:06:30.611
You must know something.

00:06:30.736 --> 00:06:31.737
It's green.

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:32.988
Oh, no!

00:06:35.073 --> 00:06:39.494
You can tell me. We're still friends,
even though you dumped me in college.

00:06:40.913 --> 00:06:44.917
Are you here to deal with
the Matter's activity these past few days?

00:06:45.626 --> 00:06:46.460
Yes.

00:06:46.543 --> 00:06:49.254
But you can easily give orders from Tokyo.

00:06:50.088 --> 00:06:52.215
What is the real reason you're here?

00:06:53.008 --> 00:06:54.134
<i>No way!</i>

00:06:54.301 --> 00:06:56.011
<i>Your dad died in an accident,</i>

00:06:56.094 --> 00:06:59.097
<i>and your mom and brother went missing</i>
<i>in the Burst?</i>

00:06:59.806 --> 00:07:00.807
That's crazy!

00:07:00.891 --> 00:07:01.767
Hey!

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:05.896
But you're going to save them?
You really think they're still alive?

00:07:08.482 --> 00:07:10.943
Jeez! You're so damn insensitive!

00:07:13.779 --> 00:07:14.780
This river...

00:07:17.366 --> 00:07:22.329
<i>My family often used to visit</i>
<i>the upper end of this river.</i>

00:07:22.955 --> 00:07:24.456
<i>Dad loved fishing.</i>

00:07:25.123 --> 00:07:26.166
<i>When I was little,</i>

00:07:26.249 --> 00:07:28.961
<i>I really enjoyed spending time</i>
<i>with my family,</i>

00:07:29.336 --> 00:07:30.879
<i>so I came with him.</i>

00:07:31.755 --> 00:07:36.635
<i>But I slowly got annoyed</i>
<i>at those kind of things.</i>

00:07:37.511 --> 00:07:40.806
Also, Dad got so busy with work

00:07:41.306 --> 00:07:43.642
that he hardly ever came home.

00:07:45.018 --> 00:07:48.438
But when he did come home, he would say,

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.109
"Let's go fishing, Aiko.

00:07:53.276 --> 00:07:55.153
Me, you, Mom, and Ryota,

00:07:55.946 --> 00:07:59.324
let's all go and catch a big one."

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:04.079
We never caught any big fish.

00:08:05.455 --> 00:08:08.083
When I think about it now,
I realize that

00:08:08.375 --> 00:08:12.129
he was trying to make time
with his family in his own way.

00:08:12.963 --> 00:08:14.881
But since he wasn't very social,

00:08:15.132 --> 00:08:17.467
that was all he could think of doing.

00:08:21.221 --> 00:08:24.975
It's too late now
to start wishing we could be together.

00:08:26.143 --> 00:08:29.646
It's sad I only just realized
how important they are to me.

00:08:30.605 --> 00:08:32.983
What? Important? Family?

00:08:34.234 --> 00:08:36.028
Of course! You have...

00:08:36.111 --> 00:08:37.612
No, I don't!

00:08:39.031 --> 00:08:41.783
When I was born, my dad was already gone.

00:08:41.992 --> 00:08:46.538
After I was born, my mom seized her chance
to run away with another guy.

00:08:46.747 --> 00:08:50.000
I was left behind and passed around
my relatives.

00:08:50.709 --> 00:08:53.045
I feel relieved now that I'm alone.

00:08:53.295 --> 00:08:54.963
That's <i>your</i> family, though!

00:08:55.422 --> 00:08:58.091
You ran away from your own family, right?

00:09:00.510 --> 00:09:01.845
<i>Everyone in Town knows</i>

00:09:01.928 --> 00:09:04.181
<i>you're a spoiled rich kid</i>
<i>who needed an escape.</i>

00:09:04.264 --> 00:09:05.390
<i>That's not true!</i>

00:09:05.682 --> 00:09:08.935
<i>All I wanted was to decide</i>
<i>how to live my own life!</i>

00:09:09.102 --> 00:09:12.105
<i>I was sick of people bragging about </i>
<i>happiness and misfortune!</i>

00:09:12.189 --> 00:09:14.107
That's what an escape is.

00:09:14.191 --> 00:09:18.445
I had an arm eaten off by Matter
and got an artificial organism arm!

00:09:19.029 --> 00:09:21.782
Who's bragging
about misfortune now, loser?

00:09:22.115 --> 00:09:25.744
You special ordered a new arm
made from artificial organisms!

00:09:25.827 --> 00:09:27.746
You're still a spoiled rich kid!

00:09:27.913 --> 00:09:29.247
Having fun out here?

00:09:29.915 --> 00:09:32.250
Quit fighting and get some rest.

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:33.627
Sagami...

00:09:34.252 --> 00:09:36.004
Stay on your guard.

00:09:36.254 --> 00:09:40.092
Right now, who knows
what might happen inside the Area?

00:09:40.675 --> 00:09:43.970
<i>You can't know what's going on</i>
<i>until you're on-site.</i>

00:09:44.137 --> 00:09:46.264
<i>But without going inside the Area,</i>

00:09:46.348 --> 00:09:48.600
<i>the information we can get is limited.</i>

00:09:49.184 --> 00:09:51.269
Aren't you sending in a recon team?

00:09:51.394 --> 00:09:53.730
The Area is completely
sealed off now.

00:09:54.231 --> 00:09:56.525
Not a single person can get in.

00:09:57.109 --> 00:09:59.778
Not a single person, huh?

00:10:03.949 --> 00:10:07.828
<i>It looks like the neutralizer</i>
<i>you injected Aiko with is working.</i>

00:10:08.411 --> 00:10:10.539
Make sure the Divers don't find out.

00:10:10.872 --> 00:10:13.583
Most Divers know Matter is attracted

00:10:13.667 --> 00:10:16.920
to biologically active substances
excreted by a composite

00:10:17.003 --> 00:10:19.047
of real and artificial organisms.

00:10:19.798 --> 00:10:21.091
I know that much.

00:10:22.092 --> 00:10:23.510
Can I ask you something?

00:10:24.594 --> 00:10:28.390
How do you think the Matter was created?

00:10:29.182 --> 00:10:32.894
Aiko Tachibana was in an accident.
The treatment that split her

00:10:33.145 --> 00:10:37.315
set off abnormal artificial cell
proliferation in the duplicate body.

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:40.652
That's all I can say for certain.

00:10:40.735 --> 00:10:41.862
What was the cause?

00:10:42.237 --> 00:10:45.115
Was it a warning
not to attempt something taboo?

00:10:45.615 --> 00:10:47.868
It has nothing to do with any of that.

00:10:48.285 --> 00:10:52.455
We simply didn't know enough
about what artificial organisms could do.

00:10:53.206 --> 00:10:56.042
You mean even Toshihide Yura
didn't know enough?

00:10:56.334 --> 00:10:57.711
That's what I'm saying.

00:10:58.336 --> 00:11:01.965
So, what are you going to do
with her fake body?

00:11:02.549 --> 00:11:04.050
Return it where it belongs.

00:11:04.718 --> 00:11:06.386
And let his creation live?

00:11:06.845 --> 00:11:09.514
Will that atone
for the sin Yura committed?

00:11:10.098 --> 00:11:11.516
Don't worry about that.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:14.019
Even if we don't know the cause,

00:11:14.394 --> 00:11:17.272
putting things back the way they were
is a simple process.

00:11:17.397 --> 00:11:18.648
Simulations show...

00:11:18.732 --> 00:11:20.275
I'm not asking that.

00:11:20.901 --> 00:11:24.195
Her brain and body
function just like a real person.

00:11:24.821 --> 00:11:28.533
Can you really say that
her replica is not human?

00:11:28.617 --> 00:11:30.911
She is clearly not human.

00:11:31.328 --> 00:11:32.579
She's no more than...

00:11:35.248 --> 00:11:37.918
I've finished refitting
the Bipod batteries.

00:11:38.001 --> 00:11:38.919
Daisuke.

00:11:39.294 --> 00:11:42.964
I'll have everyone load all
the vial cartridges in here later.

00:11:44.132 --> 00:11:47.385
From here on,
Matter activity will continue to rise.

00:11:47.552 --> 00:11:50.513
Even so, do you still want to go?

00:11:55.143 --> 00:11:57.312
So, who is he?

00:11:57.395 --> 00:11:58.229
What?

00:11:58.813 --> 00:12:00.231
Who is Yuya Kanzaki?

00:12:01.942 --> 00:12:04.110
-A classmate.
-A classmate?

00:12:04.611 --> 00:12:07.405
Actually, I don't know him that well.

00:12:07.572 --> 00:12:08.448
Really?

00:12:08.823 --> 00:12:11.242
He transferred just before summer break.

00:12:11.534 --> 00:12:13.328
That's when I first met him.

00:12:13.536 --> 00:12:16.081
I was brought to you guys
right after that,

00:12:16.164 --> 00:12:19.000
and now we're all going to Primary Point.

00:12:19.084 --> 00:12:22.128
What? Are you kidding?
That's totally fishy!

00:12:22.337 --> 00:12:24.923
Why go to such a dangerous place with him?

00:12:26.800 --> 00:12:27.884
Kazuki!

00:12:28.385 --> 00:12:31.554
Divers never get involved in
their client's business.

00:12:31.638 --> 00:12:34.808
I know that!
But this isn't a normal retrieval!

00:12:34.891 --> 00:12:38.520
It's exactly the same.
Isn't that right, client?

00:12:40.605 --> 00:12:41.940
Shinoyama said to move

00:12:42.023 --> 00:12:45.235
all personal belongings
from the Bipods to the Beetle,

00:12:45.819 --> 00:12:49.739
and he'll be taking over guard duty
for Sagami in one hour.

00:12:53.827 --> 00:12:56.454
As a thank you,
I'll give you a warning.

00:12:56.955 --> 00:13:00.625
Don't get any more involved with
what's happening in the Area.

00:13:02.711 --> 00:13:05.755
You see, I'd like to remain
good friends forever.

00:13:05.839 --> 00:13:06.840
Bye.

00:13:18.268 --> 00:13:21.021
I hardly looked inside
before bringing this.

00:13:21.104 --> 00:13:22.147
SUMMER NOTEBOOK TWO

00:13:22.731 --> 00:13:23.857
I'm such an idiot.

00:13:26.735 --> 00:13:29.154
Oh, this is...

00:13:36.619 --> 00:13:38.329
<i>Happy birthday.</i>

00:13:40.331 --> 00:13:42.542
Do you want some help, Aiko?

00:13:42.709 --> 00:13:43.793
I'm okay!

00:13:49.132 --> 00:13:50.091
What?

00:13:50.383 --> 00:13:52.010
-What?
-What happened?

00:13:52.677 --> 00:13:53.595
What is it?

00:13:53.678 --> 00:13:58.767
<i>Unidentified living organism detected</i>
<i>in North Block storage area.</i>

00:13:58.850 --> 00:13:59.809
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:14:02.353 --> 00:14:03.688
What happened?

00:14:10.487 --> 00:14:11.363
What?

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:19.537
That's a sample organism that
Holos Habilis gave to a few customers.

00:14:19.621 --> 00:14:23.833
Holos Habilis?
That's the company Dad worked for.

00:14:24.584 --> 00:14:26.920
So, this thing is yours, Aiko?

00:14:27.045 --> 00:14:30.090
But when I dropped it, it was just a ball.

00:14:31.049 --> 00:14:32.425
It was in storage mode.

00:14:32.842 --> 00:14:34.844
Did the electric shock wake you up?

00:14:34.928 --> 00:14:36.346
Must be an exposed wire.

00:14:36.471 --> 00:14:37.597
It's from your dad?

00:14:37.931 --> 00:14:41.059
Yes. It was a birthday present.

00:14:41.935 --> 00:14:45.522
But the accident happened
right after that,

00:14:46.147 --> 00:14:48.525
so I never found out what it was.

00:14:49.025 --> 00:14:50.110
Hey!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:52.487
-What's its name?
-Huh?

00:14:52.570 --> 00:14:53.738
Doesn't have one?

00:14:54.239 --> 00:14:57.951
I just found out it's a living creature.

00:14:58.243 --> 00:15:00.245
It's very valuable.

00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:04.874
This Holos type is an artificially created
complete living organism.

00:15:05.375 --> 00:15:09.421
What?
Its whole body is an artificial organism?

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:12.841
Its development was suspended
after the Burst.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:15.552
I didn't know there were prototypes.

00:15:18.221 --> 00:15:19.722
My body

00:15:20.014 --> 00:15:24.602
is made of the same stuff as the Live Suit
and this animal, right?

00:15:25.103 --> 00:15:25.979
Yes.

00:15:26.062 --> 00:15:30.483
Since your whole body is
made from artificial organisms,

00:15:30.942 --> 00:15:34.154
both you and that sample
are extremely precious.

00:15:35.196 --> 00:15:37.282
You make us sound like objects.

00:15:37.699 --> 00:15:38.867
You are.

00:15:38.950 --> 00:15:41.202
No, to be more precise,

00:15:41.411 --> 00:15:44.789
you're a system
for artificially creating life.

00:15:45.415 --> 00:15:46.875
That's not what I meant.

00:15:47.459 --> 00:15:48.585
But it's the truth.

00:15:48.918 --> 00:15:51.254
The system that gives you life

00:15:51.337 --> 00:15:53.882
is something humans
have wanted a long time.

00:15:53.965 --> 00:15:54.966
Stop it!

00:15:56.217 --> 00:15:58.470
You don't understand, Kanzaki!

00:16:02.432 --> 00:16:03.808
Um...

00:16:03.892 --> 00:16:06.186
I'll be taking over for Sagami soon,

00:16:06.519 --> 00:16:09.230
so if you're done
with the Live Suit repairs...

00:16:16.154 --> 00:16:17.155
It can't be.

00:16:17.405 --> 00:16:21.409
Nobody wants their body
to be like a monster.

00:16:43.723 --> 00:16:44.557
A present?

00:16:50.813 --> 00:16:54.692
<i>If Kurose takes over</i>
<i>as the company head after Dr. Kiryu,</i>

00:16:55.109 --> 00:16:57.862
<i>he's sure to stop</i>
<i>Cell Assembler Two research</i>

00:16:58.071 --> 00:17:01.199
until the Burst is brought to an end.

00:17:02.075 --> 00:17:06.204
I won't allow this country's economy
to be ruined any more.

00:17:06.829 --> 00:17:08.540
I agree with you.

00:17:09.207 --> 00:17:12.502
We shouldn't slow the progress
of Kiryu Research.

00:17:13.086 --> 00:17:15.547
So, I'm doing something about it.

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:18.841
-No luck!
-I can't find her!

00:17:18.925 --> 00:17:20.802
Why did you leave her alone?

00:17:20.927 --> 00:17:23.721
This is bad!
A contamination suit is gone.

00:17:23.805 --> 00:17:24.722
-What?
-What?

00:17:26.015 --> 00:17:29.519
<i>Matter activity detected near facility.</i>

00:17:30.812 --> 00:17:33.648
We have to do something.
I have to tell Daisuke.

00:17:33.898 --> 00:17:36.150
Hey! Where are you?

00:17:36.693 --> 00:17:38.236
Where are you?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.497
Hey! Where did you go?

00:17:55.044 --> 00:17:57.380
Where are you, Tachibana?

00:17:58.381 --> 00:18:00.550
That doesn't hurt.

00:18:01.718 --> 00:18:02.594
Of course not.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:07.890
I was saved by the same stuff
that little guy is made of.

00:18:09.642 --> 00:18:11.227
If not, then I'd be...

00:18:16.608 --> 00:18:18.610
Where am I?

00:18:25.241 --> 00:18:28.453
No, I still haven't found her.
I'll look a little...

00:18:31.706 --> 00:18:35.376
Even if it's safe around here,
you can't go out on your own.

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:37.962
We don't want to risk lives over this.

00:18:38.338 --> 00:18:39.172
I'm sorry.

00:18:40.632 --> 00:18:42.425
I admit you're pretty brave.

00:18:43.468 --> 00:18:47.639
You're going to a place
most Divers would never come close to.

00:18:49.724 --> 00:18:51.351
So, you should understand him.

00:18:52.018 --> 00:18:53.853
Like you, he's doing his best

00:18:54.187 --> 00:18:57.565
to move on with life
while carrying a huge burden.

00:18:59.692 --> 00:19:01.527
We may not know who he is,

00:19:01.819 --> 00:19:05.448
but you can at least understand
that much about him.

00:19:09.327 --> 00:19:10.620
It's a snow grouse!

00:19:10.953 --> 00:19:14.999
Oh, Dad! Don't film me!
Film the snow grouse!

00:19:15.208 --> 00:19:17.043
Give it to me, Dad!

00:19:19.212 --> 00:19:25.218
Today, Dr. Yura, Dad, and I came
to Murodo together.

00:19:26.511 --> 00:19:30.723
<i>Dr. Yura, do you like the lunch</i>
<i>that I made?</i>

00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:33.768
<i>I knew you'd like it!</i>

00:19:33.851 --> 00:19:37.772
<i>Maybe I'll become your wife one day..</i>

00:19:38.815 --> 00:19:39.816
Yuzuha.

00:19:40.566 --> 00:19:44.946
Even Yura couldn't bring you
out of your coma.

00:19:45.571 --> 00:19:49.283
All that stuff about the Yura Notes
must be a lie.

00:19:50.243 --> 00:19:53.079
As your father,
I promise to bring you back.

00:19:55.748 --> 00:19:56.749
Aiko!

00:19:58.251 --> 00:20:00.628
I'm very sorry, everyone.

00:20:01.254 --> 00:20:03.381
Well, at least we found you.

00:20:03.506 --> 00:20:06.676
Be more careful!
It's not just your life at risk.

00:20:06.759 --> 00:20:07.802
Hey!

00:20:09.303 --> 00:20:10.513
Where is Kanzaki?

00:20:11.723 --> 00:20:12.765
You found her?

00:20:15.184 --> 00:20:16.102
Thank goodness.

00:20:21.107 --> 00:20:23.401
I'm sorry. If I...

00:20:25.236 --> 00:20:26.738
If I died...

00:20:27.739 --> 00:20:30.700
I wouldn't be able to save
Mom and Ryota, would I?

00:20:32.201 --> 00:20:35.913
I can only save them if I'm still alive.

00:20:41.502 --> 00:20:42.795
This is precious, right?

00:20:45.965 --> 00:20:46.799
Yes.

00:20:50.803 --> 00:20:51.721
I'm sorry.

00:20:52.555 --> 00:20:54.265
Thank you, Kanzaki.

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:01.147
Hey, is Gummi on board?

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:02.356
Gummi?

00:21:02.982 --> 00:21:06.611
That's its name
because it's like gummy candy.

00:21:07.195 --> 00:21:08.237
Looks yummy, no?

00:21:08.404 --> 00:21:09.405
So random...

00:21:09.489 --> 00:21:11.157
-I like it!
-You do?

00:21:12.116 --> 00:21:13.326
It's cute!

00:21:13.409 --> 00:21:14.577
I told you.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.748
Last night's alarm

00:21:18.831 --> 00:21:22.585
was because Matter activity
was detected near K2.

00:21:23.252 --> 00:21:24.587
It's gotten this far?

00:21:25.087 --> 00:21:29.425
It must be up to the K2 gate.
We can't let our guard down.

00:21:30.009 --> 00:21:31.594
Is everyone ready?

00:21:32.386 --> 00:21:33.346
-Wilco!
-Wilco!

00:21:33.429 --> 00:21:34.555
Here we go!

00:21:56.327 --> 00:21:57.829
Special comms vehicles

00:21:57.995 --> 00:22:02.208
<i>have just passed through Aimoto Dam</i>
<i>and entered Area One.</i>

00:22:02.792 --> 00:22:05.127
I got it. Thank you.

00:22:12.093 --> 00:22:15.596
<i>Today's topic is a breach of trust</i>
<i>by Susumu Kurose,</i>

00:22:15.680 --> 00:22:17.682
head of the Kurose Research Lab.

00:22:18.266 --> 00:22:23.563
He is accused of misappropriation of funds
and corporate embezzlement.

00:22:25.189 --> 00:22:28.067
Then, let us begin.

00:23:56.864 --> 00:23:58.950
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
